            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "chef24"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent show stopping flavor - super easy to make too! I used two Tbsp. rose water.",
            "datePublished": "2017-11-18T02:27:30.300Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Auntie ji"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very nice ice cream. I made it to take to a Diwali dinner.\nI used Haagen Daz vanilla 1 qt and 1 pint. I did not have cardamom, which I somehow ran out of, so I omitted it. \nI used one large Tbls of rose syrup as I was afraid it would be too sweet. I used a small pinch of saffron and I finely chopped the roasted and salted pistachios (from a package), thinking a bit of salt would enhance flavor, before adding into the softened ice cream. It is now sitting in a soufflé dish in the freezer. I tasted it after it was all mixed together and I am glad I cutback on the rose syrup. I think the next time I'll use a full pinch of saffron and the cardomom for sure. I imagine I'll need to dry out the rose petals first and will add them tomorrow with a light dusting of pistachios on the ice cream.\nMaybe a 5 star but since I've not tasted it frozen it'll be 4 for now. Very pretty with very little effort.",
            "datePublished": "2017-10-18T20:57:43.627Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Novin"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added some saffron to the ice cream and it turned great! Worth trying it!",
            "datePublished": "2016-07-24T21:51:44.613Z"
          },
          {
